body:
## Objective

Implement Stage 8 of the accepted StrideBrain v0.1 sequence: convert an authorized Stage 6/7 comparison insight into one explicitly reviewed, idempotent, auditable internal review action.

This is the first bounded `Think → Do` transition in the customer-facing product.

The only business-changing action in this stage is:

> **Create an internal review action linked to the active project, immutable comparison result, structured claims, and supporting evidence.**

The system may prepare a proposal, but it may not create business state until an authorized user reviews and explicitly confirms it.

## Governing contracts

- `docs/build/IMPLEMENTATION_SEQUENCE.md` — Stage 8
- `docs/decisions/ADR-004-first-governed-action.md`
- `docs/build/V0_1_BUILD_CONTRACT.md`
- `docs/build/SHARED_DTO_AND_STATE_CONTRACT.md`
- `docs/architecture/AUTHORIZATION_MODEL_V0_1.md`
- `docs/architecture/EVIDENCE_AND_AUTHORITY_MODEL.md`
- Stage 3 Project Workspace, Stage 4 comparison, Stage 5 economics, Stage 6 comparison experience, and Stage 7 evidence panel merged into `main`

## Primary user flow

From the authorized Xinyi comparison:

1. select `Create internal review action`;
2. server reopens the authorized immutable Stage 4 comparison and Stage 5 economics result;
3. server prepares or reopens one bounded `ProposedAction` using verified structured claims only;
4. review sheet shows title, rationale, evidence, uncertainty, suggested assignee, and due date;
5. user may edit title and rationale without removing mandatory warnings/evidence statements;
6. user may choose an authorized assignee and due date;
7. user explicitly confirms `Create internal review action`;
8. server re-resolves trusted `RuntimeContext` and rechecks permissions, project state, run freshness, evidence access, assignee eligibility, and idempotency;
9. one transaction creates `Action`, evidence links, and append-only `AuditEvent`, and consumes the proposal;
10. application returns a durable `ActionReceipt` and shows the action in the Project Workspace without losing comparison context.

No external communication, quote approval, supplier contact, customer response, financial mutation, or model-directed write occurs.

## Policy version

```text
INTERNAL-REVIEW-ACTION-1.0
```

## Canonical Horizon action

### Default title

```text
Validate imported-stone and lighting assumptions for Xinyi quote v3
```

### Required rationale content

The prepared rationale must include only verified structured facts:

- imported-stone forecast variance versus eligible reconciled actual history;
- lighting quoted-price variance and the insufficient reconciled-actual evidence state;
- accelerated programme difference with no supported quantified premium;
- comparison/enrichment run references;
- mandatory evidence/uncertainty wording.

It must not say that the quote is wrong, a supplier is overcharging, or the programme caused a specific premium.

## ProposedAction contract

A proposal is reviewable preparatory state, not an executed business action.

Required fields include:

- opaque business key;
- organization and project scope;
- comparison run and enrichment run linkage;
- type `INTERNAL_REVIEW`;
- title and rationale;
- mandatory rationale fragments/warnings;
- suggested assignee;
- suggested due date;
- exact authorized evidence references and claim keys;
- policy version;
- source/input/permission/result fingerprints;
- created-by source (`SYSTEM`, `USER`, or future `MODEL_ASSISTED`);
- status and expiry;
- created/updated timestamps.

Preparation must be deterministic in v0.1 and require no model.

## Review/edit contract

Before confirmation, an authorized user may:

- edit title within bounded length/content rules;
- edit rationale while mandatory verified statements and uncertainty warnings remain present;
- select an eligible organization assignee;
- set or clear a due date within policy bounds;
- inspect linked Stage 7 evidence;
- cancel/abandon the proposal.

The UI must use explicit language:

```text
Create internal review action
建立內部審查事項
```

Vague controls such as `Approve AI`, `Run agent`, or `Execute` are prohibited.

## Assignee policy

An assignee candidate must:

- belong to the same organization;
- be active;
- be eligible for internal review assignment;
- have access to the active project under the reviewed assignment policy;
- not be selected from a browser-supplied organization or role;
- remain eligible at confirmation time.

A user without `action:assign` may accept the policy-provided default only when explicitly permitted by the service, and may not browse or choose arbitrary people.

## Authorization

Required server capabilities:

- proposal: `action:internal-review:propose`;
- creation: `action:internal-review:create`;
- changing assignee: `action:assign`.

Additional checks:

- user can access the active project;
- project assignment permits action creation;
- comparison and enrichment runs belong to the project and organization;
- user can currently access every mandatory claim/evidence source;
- Viewer is denied before sensitive proposal/evidence reads;
- selected assignee is valid for organization/project;
- project is not deleted or closed to new actions by policy;
- proposal is prepared, unexpired, and unconsumed.

Cross-tenant, malformed, inaccessible, or downgraded contexts must return neutral safe outcomes without hidden IDs/counts.

## Staleness and fingerprint recheck

Confirmation must compare stored proposal fingerprints against current authoritative state, including at minimum:

- active quote version;
- comparison input/result/policy versions;
- economics enrichment source/input/permission/structural fingerprints;
- relevant claim/evidence authority, conflict, freshness, and supersession state;
- active project state;
- current user permissions;
- assignee eligibility.

Material change returns `STALE_COMPARISON` or `REFRESH_REQUIRED` and creates no Action.

No task may be created from stale or materially changed intelligence.

## Idempotency

The confirmation command requires a server-validated idempotency key.

Required behavior:

- identical retry returns the existing durable receipt;
- same key with different payload is rejected;
- concurrent retries create one Action only;
- proposal may be consumed once;
- unique database constraints protect the invariant below the application layer.

## Atomic transaction

One database transaction must create/update:

- `Action`;
- action-to-evidence linkage (normalized relation or immutable authorized evidence snapshot according to the accepted schema decision);
- append-only `AuditEvent`;
- consumed/confirmed `ProposedAction` state;
- idempotency record/receipt state where required.

Simulated failure at any point must leave no partial action, evidence link, audit event, or consumed proposal.

## Audit event

Successful creation records:

- actor user/membership;
- organization and project;
- proposed-action and action business keys;
- comparison/enrichment run and policy versions;
- evidence and claim references;
- original proposal fields;
- final edited fields;
- assignee and due date;
- request/correlation/idempotency identifiers;
- timestamp and successful result.

Denied/failed attempts produce a safe operator trace without exposing sensitive details to the end user.

Audit events are append-only.

## ActionReceipt

A successful response and receipt view must include only permission-safe data:

- action business key;
- title;
- project;
- assignee display name or unassigned state;
- due date;
- status `OPEN`;
- created timestamp;
- created-by display;
- source comparison/enrichment references;
- linked evidence count only when authorized;
- link back to comparison/evidence;
- link to the project action list.

A toast alone is insufficient.

## Project Workspace integration

After creation:

- the action appears in the active project’s Actions surface/summary;
- the receipt remains reopenable under current authorization;
- comparison route, selected projects, locale, and evidence context are preserved;
- refresh/back/forward must not create duplicates;
- no fake action appears on failure.

## Required outcomes

### Proposal

- `PREPARED`
- `PROPOSAL_UNAVAILABLE`
- `PROPOSAL_EXPIRED`
- `PROPOSAL_STALE`
- `PROPOSAL_NOT_AUTHORIZED`
- safe `PROPOSAL_FAILED`

### Confirmation

- `CREATED`
- `IDEMPOTENT_REPLAY`
- `ACTION_NOT_AUTHORIZED`
- `ASSIGNEE_UNAVAILABLE`
- `EVIDENCE_UNAVAILABLE`
- `STALE_COMPARISON`
- `PROPOSAL_EXPIRED`
- `PROPOSAL_ALREADY_CONSUMED`
- `IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT`
- safe `ACTION_CREATE_FAILED`

## Bilingual and accessibility requirements

- complete English/Taiwan Traditional Chinese parity for proposal, edit, confirmation, validation, stale, denied, duplicate, failure, and receipt states;
- explicit confirmation button and irreversible-effect explanation;
- semantic form labels and error associations;
- keyboard-operable review sheet;
- focus moves to first validation error or receipt heading;
- focus returns safely on cancel;
- due date accessible without pointer-only interaction;
- warnings are text-plus-icon, not color-only;
- mobile full-height review/receipt mode;
- reduced-motion support;
- no English backend/provider/policy plumbing in normal Chinese mode.

## Performance target

For the seeded controlled demo:

- proposal open p95 target: ≤500 ms after Stage 6/7 result is available;
- action confirmation p95 target: ≤800 ms excluding network transit;
- bounded repository calls;
- no model call;
- no per-evidence or per-assignee N+1 waterfall;
- measured PostgreSQL/browser baseline recorded.

## Required tests

- authorized Project Manager/Estimator prepares and creates the canonical action;
- Viewer proposal/create direct UI and API paths are denied before sensitive reads/writes;
- cross-organization project, comparison, proposal, assignee, action, and evidence identifiers are rejected;
- proposal uses only immutable verified Stage 5 claims/evidence;
- title/rationale edit validation preserves mandatory warnings;
- stale quote/run/economics/evidence/permission/assignee states reject creation;
- unauthorized or missing evidence rejects creation;
- assignee organization/project eligibility enforced;
- user without assign capability cannot choose arbitrary assignee;
- idempotent retry returns the same action receipt;
- same key/different payload is rejected;
- concurrent retries create one Action;
- proposal is consumed once;
- simulated transaction failure leaves no partial records;
- Action, evidence links/snapshot, AuditEvent, and proposal consumption commit atomically;
- audit reconstructs actor, run, evidence, original/final fields, and result;
- created Action appears in Project Workspace and is reopenable;
- refresh/back/forward do not duplicate the action;
- English/Traditional Chinese parity;
- mobile/keyboard/focus behavior;
- architecture tests prevent browser/direct Prisma/model write paths;
- complete flow works with model services disabled;
- all Stage 1–7 regression, SQL, type, build, and audit gates remain green.

## Explicitly out of scope

- external email or LINE sending;
- supplier/customer communication;
- quote approval/issue;
- contract/change-order approval;
- financial/cost mutation;
- payment/accounting action;
- action completion workflow beyond safe read display;
- recurring/autonomous monitoring;
- arbitrary agent writes;
- Stage 10 model-generated proposal text;
- real customer data;
- Vercel, DNS, or live demo-domain changes.

## Deliverables

- versioned Stage 8 proposal/action/receipt contracts;
- deterministic proposal preparation service;
- authorization-aware assignee and action repositories;
- stale/fingerprint validation service;
- idempotent atomic confirmation service;
- Action/evidence/audit persistence and receipt reopen;
- proposal review sheet and durable receipt UI;
- Project Workspace action integration;
- bilingual copy and all states;
- unit, repository, transaction, concurrency, authorization, route, localization, accessibility, architecture, PostgreSQL integration, and regression tests;
- measured performance/query baseline;
- independent security/action/design review;
- implementation PR with exact-head CI evidence.

## Exit gates

- [ ] canonical authorized action succeeds with correct receipt;
- [ ] Viewer direct UI/API proposal and create are denied;
- [ ] cross-tenant identifiers leak nothing and create nothing;
- [ ] stale comparison/evidence/permissions/assignee are rejected;
- [ ] retry returns the same receipt and concurrent retry creates one action;
- [ ] simulated transaction failure creates no partial records;
- [ ] audit reconstructs actor/run/evidence/edits;
- [ ] created action appears in Project Workspace;
- [ ] bilingual/mobile/keyboard/focus behavior passes;
- [ ] proposal and confirmation meet measured performance targets;
- [ ] no external communication, approval, financial mutation, AI, deployment, or real-data behavior is added;
- [ ] all prior quality gates remain green.
